+`parseDuration(text)` is its inverse: it reads a duration written that way
+back into a number of seconds, so `parseDuration(formatSeconds(n))` is `n`.
+The text is a run of `h`, `m`, `s` and `ms` parts, in that order, each at most
+once and at least one present; each part is a number followed directly by its
+unit (so `"1h"` is `3600`, `"1m1s"` is `61`, `"0s"` is `0`, `"1h1m1s1ms"` is
